    "perio.info.button": "{{label}} – info",
    "perio.info.pd": "Probing depth — the distance in mm from the gingival margin to the base of the pocket. ≤3 mm is healthy; a deeper pocket signals inflammation/attachment loss.",
    "perio.info.gm": "Gingival margin position relative to the cemento-enamel junction (CEJ), in signed mm. Positive = gingival recession (toward the root), negative = swollen/coronal margin.",
    "perio.info.cal": "Clinical attachment level (CAL = probing depth + gingival margin) — from the CEJ to the base of the pocket; the true, reference-stable measure of attachment loss.",
    "perio.info.bop": "Bleeding on probing — an indicator of inflammation (activity). %BOP is the share of bleeding sites; <10% is healthy.",
    "perio.info.plaque": "O'Leary plaque index — presence of plaque on the tooth's 4 surfaces; PI% is the share of plaque-covered surfaces (oral hygiene).",
    "perio.info.furcation": "Furcation involvement (Glickman I–IV) at the root divergence of multi-rooted teeth; grade II–III is an aggravating factor in staging.",
    "perio.info.mobility": "Tooth mobility (Miller 0–III) — reflects attachment loss / occlusal trauma.",
    "perio.info.cej": "Detectability of the cemento-enamel junction (CEJ) — affects the accuracy of CAL/recession measurement.",
    "perio.info.rootConcavity": "Root-surface concavity; a deep concavity is harder to clean and heals less predictably.",
    "perio.info.pi": "Silness–Löe Plaque Index (0–3) per surface (mesial/distal/buccal/lingual) — grades the amount/thickness of plaque on the tooth surface, an oral-hygiene indicator.",
    "perio.info.gi": "Löe–Silness Gingival Index (0–3) per surface — grades the severity of gingival inflammation (colour, oedema, bleeding tendency).",
    "perio.info.mpi": "Mombelli modified Plaque Index (0–3) per implant surface (mesial/distal/buccal/lingual) — grade 0 no plaque, 1 plaque detectable only by running a probe across the surface, 2 plaque visible to the naked eye, 3 abundant soft deposit.",
    "perio.info.mbi": "Mombelli modified sulcus Bleeding Index (0–3) per implant surface — grade 0 no bleeding on probing, 1 isolated bleeding spots, 2 a confluent red line of blood along the margin, 3 profuse/heavy bleeding.",
    "perio.info.kg": "Width (mm) of keratinized (attached) gingiva on the tooth's buccal surface; a narrow band (<2 mm) is a mucogingival risk factor.",
    "perio.info.gt": "Gingival thickness (biotype) — a thin phenotype is more prone to recession and aesthetic complications.",
    "perio.info.miller": "Miller classification of gingival recession (I–IV) — indicates the extent of recession and the expected success of root coverage.",
